API, and then you're

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.510
able to take advantage
of autoscaling,

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.810
see the GPU utilization,
and scale these workloads up

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.550
and down based on the demand.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.490
Last, also via
Compute Engine, we

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:05.260
offer custom VM shapes, tooling,
and workflow support for you

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:08.590
to be able to scale from a
single GPU under your desk

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:12.340
to supercomputer computing
scale available on demand

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.800
with preemptible instances,
as well as committed

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.050
use discounts based
on reservations,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:20.040
to get you the best price.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.510
Our virtual machines
are available

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:24.600
in many configurations,
including predefined sizes that

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.170
align to Numa topology or,
as we've mentioned prior,

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.270
the ability to create
a custom machine type

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.480
size for your specific needs.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.760
Then you aren't having
to manage a single VM.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:40.180
You're also able to use managed
instance groups in a way

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:44.900
to control an entire fleet
of your infrastructure.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.030
You're able to
define a set of VMs

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.160
and scale up and
down as you need

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.915
or as your application requires.

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:56.570
Now let's dive into what's
new with Cloud GPUs.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.400
Within our Cloud
GPU portfolio, we

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.010
have an accelerator
for your use cases

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:13.000
from ML training and inference,
GPU-enabled HPC, CUDA Compute,

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:17.080
and GPU-accelerated
visualization.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:21.130
Our high-end offerings include
high-performance GPUs, A100s

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:25.990
and B100s, that are great
for training, inference, HPC,

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.985
and CUDA Compute.

00:06:27.985 --> 00:06:29.360
On the other end
of the spectrum,

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.470
we have T4s, which are
in more global locations,

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:36.400
providing you low latency
at a very low cost.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.160
A very common use case that
we see with our customers

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:43.480
is training and doing
inference on A100s or B100s

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:46.610
and then serving in that
global capacity on T4s.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.110
Let's take a closer look
at our A100 offering.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.840
They're available in our
accelerator-optimized VM

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.960
family, A2s, on Compute Engine.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.350
The A100s have 40
gigabits of memory.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.630
And within the VM,
you can provision up

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:11.740
to 96 Cascade Lake vCPUs
and 1.3 terabytes of memory.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:15.220
They're in fixed VM shapes to
align with the new transparent

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:16.900
Numa topology.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:21.100
And they can scale up to 16
GPUs for scale-up and scale-out

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.380
workloads, such as natural
language processing

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.650
and computer vision.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.510
But don't worry if
you don't need 16.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.790
You can go all the
way down to two GPUs

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:32.960
to be able to
easily get started.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:36.410
NVLINK fabric is the
all-to-all connectivity

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:41.330
with up to 9.6 terabytes
per second peak bandwidth.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.240
You also have the access
to advanced networking

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.840
as well as the
option for local SSD.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.570
With all these features,
you're able to achieve up

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:54.620
to 20 petaops of int8 all
within a single VM, which is

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.530
what I call mega performance.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:01.470
As I mentioned earlier,
T4s on Google Cloud

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:05.280
are able to provide a low
latency at a low cost.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:10.080
They're currently in 18 regions,
with more along the way.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.990
What's new is that we do
have flexible T4s in preview

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:13.950
currently.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:17.310
You can provision exactly
what you need for T4s

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:20.320
from vCPU and VM memory.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:23.920
We're also launching automatic
CUD renewals, Committed Use

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.470
Discounts, for GPUs.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.570
This helps reduce
cost and accidental

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:32.740
loss of your reservations.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:35.240
Now, here's what's really going
to make a difference for you

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:38.150
for being able to easily find
capacity in your selected

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:41.880
region for batch workloads.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.450
We have distribution shapes
within managed instance groups

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.620
set to Any.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.690
The way you're able to
take advantage of this

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.610
is in three very
simple, easy steps.

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:54.620
First, create a
managed instance group.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:58.100
Second, set the
distribution shape to Any.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:02.600
And three, specify your
target audience and region.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.960
Optionally, you can also
run preemptible GPUs VMs

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.310
to save money.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.320
You can take note
of any constraints

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.180
that you have, such
as supported hardware

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:14.255
in their zones or resource
quotas, to get started.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:19.740
We also have the option
for deep learning

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.530
and HPC VMs that
allows you to easily

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:25.500
get started on our
infrastructure within minutes.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.900
A simple one-click
install, and your machine

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.630
is provisioned and already
performance-optimized

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.580
on Google Cloud.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.710
It also has
compatibility-tested.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:38.310
So you have no need to worry
about the software stack.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:42.750
Simply select the CPU, GPU,
or TPU to add on to the VM.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.820
We also provide the
choice and flexibility

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.730
between different ML models,
or you have the ability

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.337
to install your own.

00:09:50.337 --> 00:09:52.670
Schrodinger's team was looking
for a cloud provider that

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.590
was just as committed
to advancing life

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:58.100
sciences and drug
discovery as they were.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.680
That's why they
chose Google Cloud.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.360
They also chose
Google because we're

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.790
known for our strength of
our network and our security

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:06.730
posture.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:09.010
The partnership
drastically changed the way

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:11.680
they were doing drug discovery.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:15.190
And as Dr. Farid said,
this could potentially

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:20.340
transform all of the way that
pharma is doing drug discovery.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.580
As with any large
resource-intensive models,

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.620
cost does start to pile up.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.840
The price per performance
worked really well for them

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.780
to create and discover
life-saving drugs

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.150
to help combat COVID.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:37.020
If they're able to do this
cost-efficiently using

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:40.650
custom types of
VMs with GPUs, then

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:44.130
think about what you'd be
able to do with your workload.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:47.460
With the change in consumer
behavior due to COVID,

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:49.770
Pagani was able to
create a virtual showroom

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.330
to allow you to
customize your own car

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.940
from the comfort of your couch.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:59.110
This virtual showroom is served
on NVIDIA T4s with the NVIDIA

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:01.900
RTX virtual workstation image.

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:05.393
