00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:49.120
Next, let's pass it up to
Omkar to cover Cloud TPUs,

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.500
what's new, and what's next.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.900
Take it away, Omkar.

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.520
OMKAR PATHAK: Thanks, Chelsie.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:57.380
We have seen
tremendous innovation

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.110
in the field of machine
learning in the past few years.

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:01.820
And we expect this
rate of innovation

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.270
to grow in the future.

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:06.690
However, this fast-paced
innovation requests

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:09.730
ever-increasing amounts
of computing power.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:11.710
As machine learning
models get more accurate,

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:14.020
they tend to get
larger, more complex,

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:17.210
and require larger data sets.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.892
This is exactly why
Google built TPUs,

00:13:19.892 --> 00:13:22.100
to accelerate the rate of
machine learning innovation

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:25.280
by delivering high performance
and by training and serving

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.830
at a very low cost.

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:29.883
TPUs are used in many
products at Google.

00:13:29.883 --> 00:13:31.550
And it's likely that
you have interacted

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:33.950
with these when you have used
some of Google's products.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:40.020
These accelerators are
available to you in Google Cloud

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:42.600
right now.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:45.390
Our goal with TPUs is to
advance machine learning

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:48.140
at Google and across the world.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:51.220
So TPUs are built for this
end-to-end user journey

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.200
of an app developer
or a researcher,

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.420
starting from fast-paced
iterative development

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:58.480
in the beginning all the way to
large-scale production training

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:01.960
and serving across a range of
machine learning use cases--

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.560
vision, language,
recommendations, and more.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.260
It's also easy to get
started with Cloud

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:11.200
TPUs with TensorFlow,
PyTorch, or JAX

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.870
in the Google Cloud
project or equivalent.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.400
You can also bring
your own models

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:19.185
or use one of our reference
models to get started.

00:14:19.185 --> 00:14:21.060
What's even more
interesting is that once you

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:22.860
get started with
Cloud TPUs, it's

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.590
easy to scale your machine
learning models on Cloud TPU

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.260
pods, which means that
you can use petaflops

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.720
of computing power with
minimal code changes.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:38.300
This image here shows
a Cloud TPU v3 pod,

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.550
which has 2,048
cores that are built

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:43.340
from the ground-up
for machine learning.

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:45.140
All of these cores
are connected together

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:48.230
with a custom-built, super-fast
interconnect, which is really

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:50.480
what delivers that
high performance when

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:54.650
you scale your machine learning
models on a Cloud TPU pod.

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:56.420
Combined with the
low cost of renting

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:59.300
Cloud TPUs on Google Cloud as
opposed to owning your own data

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:02.710
centers, this
high-performance machine

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:05.440
can unlock completely new
opportunities for innovation

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:07.900
without any upfront capital
investment on your part.

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.960
To understand the power
of easy scalability,

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:16.670
just look at our recent
results in MLPerf,

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:21.210
which is the industry standard
benchmark for ML performance.

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.730
Cloud TPUs demonstrated
leading performance numbers

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:26.080
across a range of machine
learning use cases.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:27.900
And as you can see
in the chart here,

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.750
Cloud TPUs can train some of
the common machine learning

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:33.690
reference models in
just a few seconds--

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:39.710
for example, TLRM in 38
seconds or BERT in 17 seconds.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:41.880
We believe that this
is incredibly valuable,

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:45.500
especially since large-scale
ML training has unlocked some

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.750
of the recent
breakthroughs in AI--

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:49.490
for example, lambda
in natural language

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.360
processing in multimodal models.

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:57.800
Cloud TPUs are particularly
well-suited for these kinds

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:00.410
of compute-intensive,
large-scale machine learning

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:01.010
workloads.

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:06.770
Over the last few years, we
have made relentless progress

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:08.540
on TPU hardware and software.

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:11.090
And this year, we are excited
to announce our latest

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:14.000
generation, Cloud TPU v4.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.950
On a chip-to-chip
basis, Cloud TPU v4

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:19.300
is more than twice as fast
as its previous generation.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:21.885
And at a pod scale,
Cloud TPU v4 pods

00:16:21.885 --> 00:16:24.010
take Google Cloud's machine
learning infrastructure

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.710
to a whole new level,
with more than one exaflop

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.650
of computing power
equivalent to more than 10

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:30.730
million laptops combined.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.600
We have already deployed
many of these pods

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:37.430
in Google's data
centers and will soon

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.620
have more, many of
which will be operating

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:45.370
at or near 90%
carbon-free energy.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:47.980
Cloud TPU v4 pods will be
available to our Google Cloud

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:53.920
customers in
preview in Q4, 2021.

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:56.050
Now, it's not just
the sheer computing

00:16:56.050 --> 00:17:00.340
power that pushes machine
learning innovation forward.

00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:02.710
We believe that making
the system easy to use

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:06.020
is just as important as well.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:08.290
And so we recently launched
a completely new software

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:11.050
architecture that helps you
interact much more easily

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:15.119
and much more seamlessly
with Cloud TPUs.

00:17:15.119 --> 00:17:19.050
With Cloud TPU VMs, you can
now drag full Cloud TPU parts

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:21.938
directly from your desks
for the first time.

00:17:21.938 --> 00:17:23.980
It's like having a machine
learning supercomputer

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.359
under your desk.

00:17:26.359 --> 00:17:29.930
With Cloud TPU VMs, we aim to
make interactive supercomputing

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:31.830
attainable to our users.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:33.740
And it's been incredibly
encouraging to see

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.960
positive feedback from
our early customers.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.870
For example, Hugging Face,
which is a leading open source

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.930
provider of NLP technologies,
recently integrated

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:46.730
JAX, along with
TensorFlow and PyTorch,

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.790
in their popular
Transformers library.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.220
And they were able to
pre-train a base-sized BERT

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:56.090
model in less than a day with
just eight cores of v3, which

00:17:56.090 --> 00:18:00.430
is the smallest
reservable unit of a pod.

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:02.210
Similarly, our
users at Gridspace,

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:04.390
which provides contact
center automation

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:07.510
tools, such as low-latency
speech analytics,

00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:09.640
were able to train both
speech and language

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:14.230
models with an immediate
2x performance improvement.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:17.590
They were also able to scale
these models on Cloud TPU parts

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:18.745
with no code changes.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.370
These usability and
performance benefits

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:26.040
make it much easier than
ever before to get started

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.530
with Cloud TPUs and scale
your machine learning models

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:29.700
on Cloud TPU pods.

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:34.480
Along with this powerful
user experience,

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:36.580
Cloud TPUs also support
all the major machine

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:40.450
learning frameworks, including
TensorFlow, PyTorch, and JAX.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:42.640
We encourage you to
check out these links

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.800
and try out our reference
models and tutorials.

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:50.240
In summary, at Google
Cloud, we believe

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:52.640
that cutting-edge machine
learning infrastructure

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:57.030
should excel at performance,
usability, and scalability.

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.450
So we'll continue to invest
in making our systems

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:01.730
more easy to use,
enterprise-class,

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:04.550
and open and pervasive.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:07.310
Hopefully, with all of these
updates on Cloud GPUs and Cloud

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:10.280
TPUs, our cutting-edge machine
learning infrastructure

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:13.250
is much more accessible and much
more useful to you than ever

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.320
before.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:16.980
Thank you.

